/* The pager stays IN FLOW after the table (card 20260921_22): a sticky
   bottom pin on this unbounded workspace floats the bar mid-list at rest,
   covering 13-14 of 20 rows. List-end flow leaves every row visible.
   SIL-572 (2026-10-29): the pager is ALSO an opaque, elevated surface —
   QA measured row kebabs (the pinned rail's ⋯ triggers) sharing pixels with
   \"Trang sau\" at every scroll position, and a click at the intersection
   flipped the page instead of opening the row menu. The geometry requires
   the grid's rows to escape the bounded pane's `overflow: auto` clip — an
   engine-side clipping failure this repo cannot reproduce in Chromium (the
   pane measured flush: last row 851.6, pager top 865). The lift makes the
   clobber impossible in ANY engine: an escaped row paints UNDER the pager's
   opaque strip and never wins a click, so the kebab can never press over the
   pager and the pager can never steal the kebab's tap, scrolled or not. */
.dispatch-plan-page__workspace > .ds-pagination {
  position: relative;
  z-index: calc(var(--z-base, 1) + 1);
  background: var(--bg);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 12px 0 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color-secondary, var(--line));
}

@media (max-width: 1100px) {
  .dispatch-plan-page {
    gap: 12px;
    padding-top: 14px;
  }

  /* The shell already provides the safe outer gutter at tablet and phone
     widths. Keeping the wide operational workspace flush to that boundary
     returns a full data measure without compromising card interior spacing. */
  .dispatch-plan-page--wide {
    padding-inline: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .dispatch-plan-page__workspace {
    border-radius: var(--app-radius-md);
    padding: 12px;
  }

  .dispatch-plan-page--wide .dispatch-plan-page__workspace {
    padding: 0;
  }
}

